## Walkers (snack foods) | https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Walkers_(snack_foods) 
 It manufactures potato crisps and snack foods both under its own brand and others, and is the largest crisp manufacturer in Britain. Walkers was founded in 1948 in Leicester, England, by Henry Walker. The Walker family sold the business in 1970 to the American food producer Standard Brands. Since 1989, Walkers has been under ownership of PepsiCo, owners of the US snack brand Frito-Lay.
